"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A positive supply is how much more the vertex sends than it receives; a negative one is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"demand. There is no flow when the supplies do not sum to zero or some set of vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"supplies more than its out-edges carry. Costs may be negative, and negative cycles are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"saturated. A self-loop carries its capacity when its cost is negative and nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise. Capacities may be of an unsigned type, up to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int.max","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Computed by the network simplex with block-search pivots and strongly feasible trees.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Which optimum is returned when several exist is unspecified, but the same input always","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gives the same result. ","type":"text"},{"code":"supply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once per vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, then, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each edge in position order, ","type":"text"},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and then ","type":"text"},{"code":"cost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", before any work.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every capacity is at least zero; capacities, supplies and costs fit in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; Σ capacity × |cost| fits in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Cost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (checked before solving, since it bounds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"total cost); 4(n + 1)(the greatest |cost| of a non-loop edge + 1) fits in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solver’s artificial cost, with room for its potentials and reduced costs); the positive","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"supplies sum within ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/minimumcostflow(supply:capacity:cost:)"]}],"references":{"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)":{"title":"minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A least-cost flow within capacities that meets every supply, or nil when there is none.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumCostFlow"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"supply"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"capacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","p